<section class="w-full py-16 bg-white text-neutral-700 font-sans">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 flex flex-col gap-12">
        
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-3xl/10 font-display font-black text-neutral-900 tracking-tight sm:text-4xl/12">
                Our Team Of Pastors
            </h2>
            <p class="text-base/7 text-primary-500 font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
                Liderazgo de Northwest
            </p>
            <div class="w-12 h-1 bg-primary-500 mx-auto mt-1 rounded-full"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 items-start">
            
            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 rounded-church shadow-xs overflow-hidden flex flex-col h-full">
                <div class="aspect-square w-full bg-neutral-200 relative overflow-hidden group">
                    {# Espacio listo para la URL de la imagen en WP/Timber #}
                    <img src="{{ pastor_david_image_url }}" alt="David Potete" class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:scale-105">
                </div>
                <div class="p-6 flex flex-col gap-4 grow">
                    <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
                        <h3 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900">David Potete</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm/5 font-display font-semibold text-primary-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Senior Pastor</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600 flex flex-col gap-3 grow">
                        <p>
                            David chose to follow Christ at the age of 17. In 1991, after serving as a pastor in Joliet, IL, he and his family moved to the city to start Northwest Community Church as its Sr. Pastor. He has been happily married to Pam, the love of his life, since 1978. They have four children and 8 grandchildren.
                        </p>
                        <p class="italic bg-white p-3 border border-neutral-200 rounded-sm text-neutral-500">
                            <strong>His loves include:</strong> Chicago, chocolate, hotdogs (with NO ketchup), Oreos, Oreo Blizzards, running marathons, and racing up tall buildings.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-xs/5 text-neutral-500 font-medium pt-2 border-t border-neutral-200">
                            David holds undergraduate degrees in both business and pastoral administration and a Master’s degree in urban ministry.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 rounded-church shadow-xs overflow-hidden flex flex-col h-full">
                <div class="aspect-square w-full bg-neutral-200 relative overflow-hidden group">
                    {# Espacio listo para la URL de la imagen en WP/Timber #}
                    <img src="{{ pastor_tommy_image_url }}" alt="Tommy Lewis" class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:scale-105">
                </div>
                <div class="p-6 flex flex-col gap-4 grow">
                    <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
                        <h3 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900">Tommy Lewis</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm/5 font-display font-semibold text-primary-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Associate Pastor</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600 flex flex-col gap-3 grow">
                        <p>
                            Tommy Lewis has been a pastor since 1992. He has pastored in Alabama and Georgia. He was born and raised in Alabama and graduated from Welch College in 1993. Tommy met Christine at Welch College and they married in 1992.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            They have four children: Allison, Jonathan (and Lydia joined in 2018), Stephen and Joshua. They purposefully moved to Chicago to work at Northwest Community Church in 2002.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-xs/5 text-neutral-500 font-medium pt-2 border-t border-neutral-200">
                            They are thankful that God has allowed them to work at Northwest Community Church and look forward to many more years serving God in Chicago.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200 rounded-church shadow-xs overflow-hidden flex flex-col h-full">
                <div class="aspect-square w-full bg-neutral-200 relative overflow-hidden group">
                    <img src="{{ pastor_dustin_image_url }}" alt="Dustin Williams" class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:scale-105">
                </div>
                <div class="p-6 flex flex-col gap-4 grow">
                    <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
                        <h3 class="text-xl/7 font-display font-bold text-neutral-900">Dustin Williams</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm/5 font-display font-semibold text-primary-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Youth Pastor</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="text-sm/6 text-neutral-600 flex flex-col gap-3 grow">
                        <p>
                            Dustin was born and raised in Oklahoma. He accepted the call into youth ministry at 16. Since then Dustin has been involved in student ministry in numerous ways including being a camp counselor, game director, speaker, after-school teacher, children’s pastor, and teen (YUTE) pastor.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            In 2006, Dustin received his Bachelor of Arts in youth ministry with a minor in missions at Randal University in Oklahoma where he met his wife Sara. They have two children: Noah and Olivia and a dog, Mozart. Together they have been a part of Northwest Community Church since September of 2008.
                        </p>
                        <p class="italic bg-white p-3 border border-neutral-200 rounded-sm text-neutral-500">
                            <strong>Interests:</strong> Oklahoma University football, retro video games, and the TV show Survivor. You may also spot him biking to his job downtown where he works for NBC Golf even in the winter.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</section>

